/Title (The reopening of key maritime corridors in the Middle East will be a key determinant of growth in Q4. Grid connectivity emerges as another constraint, especially for energy-intensive investments in AI. Easing these constraints would support business confidence and household demand. On the other hand, continued disruption could keep costs elevated and delay new output.)
